---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import TrustMicro from '../components/TrustMicro.astro';
import FaqSection from '../components/FaqSection.astro';
import RelatedTools from '../components/RelatedTools.astro';
import TrustBlock from '../components/TrustBlock.astro';
import { sharpnessTiers } from '../data/sharpness';
import { dataSources } from '../data/sources';

const title = 'Effective Raw Calculator for MH Wilds';
const description =
  'Free MH Wilds effective raw calculator: weapon raw × affinity × Critical Boost × sharpness multiplier, step by step, with all seven sharpness tiers compared and multipliers cited. No sign-up.';

const appSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebApplication',
  '@id': 'https://hunterforge.top/eraw/#app',
  name: 'HunterForge Effective Raw Calculator',
  url: 'https://hunterforge.top/eraw',
  description: 'Effective raw calculator for Monster Hunter Wilds weapons with cited sharpness multipliers.',
  applicationCategory: 'GameApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Any',
  offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
};
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/eraw" extraSchema={[appSchema]}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Effective Raw Calculator' }]} />
  <div class="page-head">
    <p class="kicker">Tool 03</p>
    <h1>Effective Raw Calculator (ERaw)</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      ERaw turns a weapon's stats into one comparable number:
      <span class="mono">ERaw = Raw × (1 + Affinity × CritBonus) × Sharpness</span>.
      Positive affinity crits for 125% (140% at Critical Boost Lv5); negative affinity hits deal 75%.
    </p>
    <TrustMicro />
  </div>

  <div class="notice" style="margin-bottom:1.2rem;" role="note">
    <svg class="icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"></line><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"></line></svg>
    <div>
      <strong>Scope - this is a weapon-quality metric, not per-hit damage.</strong>
      True hit damage also needs motion values (per weapon attack), monster hitzones and quest modifiers,
      which vary by weapon and hunt. Use ERaw to compare weapons and skill plans on equal footing.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="builder-layout">
    <section class="card" aria-label="Inputs">
      <div class="card-title">
        <svg class="icon" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 2l-8 12h6l-2 8 10-14h-6l2-6z"/></svg>
        Weapon profile
      </div>

      <div class="field" style="margin-bottom:.8rem;">
        <label for="preset">Load a weapon preset (rarity-8 picks per class, from the snapshot)</label>
        <select id="preset"></select>
      </div>

      <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:.8rem; margin-bottom:.9rem;">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="raw">True raw</label>
          <input type="number" id="raw" min="1" max="4000" value="210" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="affinity">Affinity %</label>
          <input type="number" id="affinity" min="-100" max="100" value="15" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="field" style="margin-bottom:.9rem;">
        <label for="sharpness">Sharpness <span id="sharp-hint" class="mono" style="color:var(--ember-bright);"></span></label>
        <select id="sharpness">
          {sharpnessTiers.map((t) => (
            <option value={t.color} selected={t.color === 'white'}>
              {t.label} - ×{t.raw.toFixed(2)}
            </option>
          ))}
        </select>
      </div>

      <div class="field" style="margin-bottom:.4rem;">
        <label for="critboost">Critical Boost level <span class="mono" style="color:var(--bone-faint);">(crit damage 125% → 140%)</span></label>
        <input type="range" id="critboost" min="0" max="5" step="1" value="0" style="padding:0;" />
        <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; font-size:.7rem; color:var(--bone-faint);" class="mono">
          <span>Lv0 ×1.25</span><span>Lv5 ×1.40</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-label="Results">
      <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:0.9rem; text-align:center; padding:1.6rem 1rem;">
        <div style="font-size:.78rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.14em; color:var(--bone-faint);" class="mono">Effective raw</div>
        <div class="eraw-big" id="eraw-value">-</div>
        <div id="eraw-note" style="font-size:.85rem; color:var(--bone-dim); margin-top:.4rem;"></div>
        <ol class="eraw-steps" id="eraw-steps" style="text-align:left;"></ol>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">
          <svg class="icon" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 21h18"></path><path d="M5 21V7l7-4 7 4v14"></path></svg>
          Same weapon at every sharpness
        </div>
        <div id="sharp-compare"></div>
        <p style="font-size:.8rem; color:var(--bone-faint); margin:.8rem 0 0;">
          Sharpness multipliers - 
          {dataSources.filter((s) => s.what.includes('sharpness') || s.what.includes('Sharpness')).map((s, i) => (
            <span>{i > 0 && ' · '}<a href={s.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{s.name.replace(/ - .*/, '')}</a></span>
          ))}
          . The elemental column on the reference table below is secondary: sources disagree on the Blue value (1.05 vs 1.0625), so it's marked disputed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="tape" role="presentation"></div>

  <section aria-label="How to use the calculator">
    <h2>How to use the ERaw calculator</h2>
    <ol class="howto-steps">
      <li><strong>Enter the weapon's true raw and affinity</strong> - or load one of the 14 rarity-8 presets (one per weapon class, straight from the game files).</li>
      <li><strong>Pick the sharpness tier</strong> you actually fight at (not the top of the gauge you never reach) - each tier shows its multiplier.</li>
      <li><strong>Set Critical Boost 0–5</strong> if your build runs it; crits go from 125% to 140% damage.</li>
      <li><strong>Compare:</strong> the steps show the exact arithmetic, and the bar chart runs the same weapon across all seven tiers so you can see what sharpness is worth.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section aria-label="Worked examples" style="margin-top:1.4rem;">
    <h2>Worked examples</h2>
    <div class="example-block">
      <p style="margin:0 0 .5rem;">
        <strong>200 raw, 40% affinity, White sharpness, no Critical Boost:</strong><br />
        <span class="mono">200 × (1 + 0.40 × 0.25) × 1.32 = 200 × 1.10 × 1.32 = 290.4</span>
      </p>
      <p style="margin:0 0 .5rem;">
        <strong>250 raw, −20% affinity, Purple sharpness:</strong><br />
        <span class="mono">250 × (1 − 0.20 × 0.25) × 1.39 = 250 × 0.95 × 1.39 = 330.1</span> - negative affinity applies the fixed 0.75 crit penalty; Critical Boost is ignored.
      </p>
      <p style="margin:0;">
        <strong>200 raw, 100% affinity, White, Critical Boost Lv5:</strong><br />
        <span class="mono">200 × (1 + 1.00 × 0.40) × 1.32 = 200 × 1.40 × 1.32 = 369.6</span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-label="How the math works" style="margin-top:1.4rem;">
    <h2>How it works: formula, sources, limits</h2>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size:.95rem;">The formula</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--bone-dim); font-size:.9rem;">
          <span class="mono">ERaw = Raw × (1 + Affinity × CritBonus) × Sharpness</span> where CritBonus is
          +0.25 at Critical Boost Lv0 (crits deal 125%) and +0.40 at Lv5 (140%). Negative affinity is the
          expected-value form: a |20%| negative-affinity weapon lands 75% damage hits 20% of the time,
          for a ×0.95 factor. Every case is the same one-line expected-value calculation - shown in the steps.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size:.95rem;">Sources &amp; limitations</h3>
        <ul style="color:var(--bone-dim); font-size:.9rem; padding-left:1.1rem;">
          <li>Sharpness raw multipliers verified across Fextralife, r/MonsterHunter threads and mod documentation (Purple ×1.39, White ×1.32) - links above the chart.</li>
          <li>Critical Boost values come from the in-game skill descriptions in the game files: 125 → 128 → 131 → 134 → 137 → 140%.</li>
          <li>Out of scope on purpose: motion values, hitzones, quest modifiers and elemental damage (its sharpness column is reference-only and partially disputed).</li>
          <li>The formula implementation is unit-tested, including negative affinity and clamping.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-label="Sharpness reference table" style="margin-top:1.6rem;">
    <h2>Sharpness reference table (cited)</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap card" style="padding:.4rem;">
      <table class="data">
        <thead><tr><th>Sharpness</th><th class="num">Raw multiplier</th><th class="num">Elemental (reference)</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {sharpnessTiers.map((t) => (
            <tr>
              <td><strong>{t.label}</strong></td>
              <td class="num">×{t.raw.toFixed(2)}</td>
              <td class="num">×{t.element.toFixed(2)}</td>
              <td>{t.disputed ? <span class="badge badge--blood">sources disagree</span> : <span style="color:var(--bone-faint);">-</span>}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:.85rem; color:var(--bone-dim); margin:.8rem 0 0; max-width:75ch;">
      Wilds launched with six sharpness tiers (Red → White); Purple exists in the title-update era with a
      ×1.39 raw multiplier. White = 1.32 is confirmed by both cited wikis. Elemental multipliers feed the
      elemental part of the damage formula, which this calculator intentionally leaves out.
    </p>
  </section>

  <FaqSection
    heading="ERaw FAQ"
    items={[
      {
        q: 'What is effective raw?',
        a: 'A single number folding attack and affinity into one comparison metric: <span class="mono">Raw × (1 + Affinity × CritBonus) × Sharpness</span>. 40% affinity with base crits is worth +10% raw on average; the sharpness tier multiplies everything. Use it to compare weapons and skill plans on equal footing.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Why doesn\'t this show exact damage numbers per hit?',
        a: 'True hit damage also needs motion values (per attack animation, different for all 14 weapon types), monster hitzones and quest modifiers. A single-answer calculator without those inputs would be wrong by design - so this tool computes everything that depends on the weapon and skills, and nothing that depends on the hit.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Does negative affinity matter?',
        a: 'Yes: negative-affinity hits deal 75% damage. The calculator applies the fixed penalty and ignores Critical Boost for it (as the game does) - try −20% in the examples above.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Is purple sharpness worth much over white?',
        a: 'About 5.3% raw (×1.39 vs ×1.32). The comparison chart makes the gap visible for any weapon profile - biggest on high-raw weapons.',
      },
    ]}
  />

  <RelatedTools current="/eraw" />
  <TrustBlock />
</Base>

<script src="../scripts/eraw.ts"></script>
